Comment: 0,0:09:15.95,0:09:15.99,Default,,0,0,0,ec1sync,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.78,0:01:36.99,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Domain Expansion: Deadly Sentencing.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.29,0:01:39.00,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}A domain?!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.95,0:01:43.25,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'll take him down before he can activate it!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.63,0:01:57.85,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,All acts of violence are prohibited in this space.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.18,0:01:59.56,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,For both of us.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.56,0:02:00.60,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,For {\i1}both{\i0}?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.81,0:02:08.36,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Verbal combat, however, is another matter. {physical violence is not allowed but verbal violence i.e. arguments are allowed.}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.23,0:02:11.90,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Judgeman, please begin.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.37,0:02:17.70,Default,Judgeman,0,0,0,,Itadori Yuji
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.70,0:02:28.13,Default,Judgeman,0,0,0,,stands accused of entering the Maji Vegas gambling parlor\Nin Sendai City, Miyagi Prefecture, on July 16th, 2017,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.13,0:02:31.13,Default,Judgeman,0,0,0,,despite being under 18 at the time.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.63,0:02:32.51,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.51,0:02:34.22,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Oh.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.13,0:02:36.18,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Uhh...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.18,0:02:37.68,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Well...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.68,0:02:38.68,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Um...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.68,0:02:42.52,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Judgeman knows everything about \Nthose within this domain.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.52,0:02:45.48,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,But don't worry.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.48,0:02:48.61,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,That information isn't shared with me.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.61,0:02:52.78,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,The verdict will be decided \Nsolely by the arguments we present.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.95,0:02:56.36,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,With the exception of this evidence. {With the exception of Gojo Satoru.}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.20,0:02:59.58,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,When did you...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.95,0:03:03.58,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,This is the evidence \Nprovided by Judgeman for this case.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.00,0:03:08.08,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,There is no guarantee \Nthat this will prove the charges.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.67,0:03:11.34,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,I don't plan on telling you what it is, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.34,0:03:14.30,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,With that in mind, \Nyou must now make your case,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.30,0:03:19.05,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,clear yourself of suspicion, \Nand win a not guilty verdict from Judgeman.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.60,0:03:22.72,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}A technique based on court trials...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.73,0:03:27.90,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}That badge! He really is a lawyer?!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.31,0:03:30.86,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}He's acting more like a prosecutor, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.11,0:03:34.15,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}Higuruma is a modern sorcerer,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.15,0:03:37.16,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\fad(0,800)\i1}but this domain reminds me \Nof what {*}Master Tengen{*Tengen-sama} said.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.99,0:03:44.54,Default,Tengen,0,0,164,,{\fad(100,0)}Domains used to be a very common skill \Nfor sorcerers in the past.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.25,0:03:50.17,Default,Tengen,0,0,164,,That's because while most modern domains \Nhave a "sure-hit, sure-kill" element,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.17,0:03:53.59,Default,Tengen,0,0,164,,domains of the past lacked the "sure-kill" aspect. {omitted almost feels like the tech was always there and they chose not to use it but if that's the case then why dont people today omit it too so everyone can have a domain?} {my bad, i can't read. it's because people pushed for sure-kill and that fundamentally altered what a domain is and now they all have to live with it} {still, any reason to keep "omitted" over say "lacked"?}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.17,0:03:59.43,Default,Tengen,0,0,164,,They simply guaranteed the rules of the technique \Nwere enforced within the domain. {i'm getting a different interpretetion here: They simply guaranteed that the rules of the technique would be enforced within the domain.}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.89,0:04:03.68,Default,Tengen,0,0,164,,That used to be the standard function of domains.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.35,0:04:10.06,Default,Tengen,0,0,164,,By pushing for the "sure-kill" aspect, \Nsorcerers raised the bar for constructing a domain,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.06,0:04:16.07,Default,Tengen,0,0,164,,making it a more advanced skill that fewer people could use. {they faded out everything except tengen so let's not fade this line either}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.78,0:04:22.99,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}That means this domain isn't a "sure-kill," \Nand can't physically harm me.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.99,0:04:28.00,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}Plus, it requires some explanation of its rules, \Njust like a Binding Vow.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.04,0:04:32.50,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,You get one chance to make a statement.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.50,0:04:34.30,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,This applies to both of us, as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.75,0:04:39.80,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,After your statement, I get one chance \Nto make my rebuttal based on this evidence.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.80,0:04:45.10,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Judgeman will then deliver the verdict \Nin accordance with the Six Codes.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.85,0:04:47.68,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,What happens if I'm judged guilty?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.31,0:04:52.31,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Unfortunately, I have no obligation \Nto answer that question.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.31,0:04:55.94,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,However, I will tell you this.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.11,0:04:59.03,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,You have three options:
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.61,0:05:00.49,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Silence.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.49,0:05:01.36,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Confession.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.36,0:05:02.87,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Denial.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.87,0:05:05.91,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Your denial may include false statements.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.91,0:05:08.50,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,You mean I can just lie?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.00,0:05:10.37,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,In court?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.00,0:05:15.71,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,If everyone told the truth, \Nthere would be no need for trials.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.88,0:05:19.72,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Now, make your argument.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.72,0:05:22.01,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Judgeman is not very patient.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.43,0:05:30.27,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}I did go to that gambling place. \NI played a few rounds. I might've even won.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.73,0:05:34.44,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}I can't avoid lying if I want to claim innocence. {plead not guilty} {would yuji use legal terminology tho}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.44,0:05:37.40,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}In that case, what I need to consider is...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.78,0:05:39.49,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}what's in that evidence!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.65,0:05:44.99,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\an8}There is no guarantee \Nthat this will prove the charges.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.37,0:05:50.71,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}One: if the evidence doesn't prove I entered the parlor,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.71,0:05:52.50,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}I just need to deny it or remain silent.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.83,0:05:57.04,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}Two: if the evidence only proves I entered,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.04,0:05:59.80,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}should I try an excuse that would earn leniency?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.59,0:06:03.47,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}But if the evidence is a bust,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.47,0:06:07.89,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'd be digging my own grave by admitting it...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.89,0:06:13.31,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}Three: if the evidence proves \NI not only entered, but actually played,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.31,0:06:15.02,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'm basically screwed.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.04,0:05:53.83,Default,Yuji,0,0,164,,{\an8}No!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.17,0:06:01.59,Default,Yuji,0,0,164,,{\an8}I just went to the bathroom.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.59,0:06:03.47,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,{\an8}So you did enter it, then!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.47,0:06:05.14,Default,Yuji,0,0,164,,{\an8}Y-Yes...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.35,0:06:16.31,Default,Yuji,0,0,164,,{\an8}I'm sorry...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.31,0:06:19.36,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}Should I bet on confessing to get a lighter sentence?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.36,0:06:22.53,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}Does this court even have such a concept?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.99,0:06:28.87,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,I did enter the Maji Vegas gambling parlor,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.41,0:06:33.04,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,but only because I suddenly needed to poop \Nand had to use their bathroom!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.37,0:06:35.54,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Is that so?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.92,0:06:37.63,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'm ditching option three!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.63,0:06:41.17,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}I don't know if this court \Naccepts extenuating circumstances,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.17,0:06:43.55,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}but this will leave the best impression!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.55,0:06:45.18,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}I think!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.18,0:06:48.18,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,My turn, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.89,0:06:56.23,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,This is from a second-hand dealer \Nnear Maji Vegas on the day in question. {we got so many translations for this: cash exchange, second-hand shop, thrift shop, and now antique shop, with cr being the most "out there" as always idk where they got that from}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.31,0:07:01.32,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,In essence, it's an image from \Nthe security camera of a cash exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.40,0:07:10.79,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Would you agree the appearance and build\Nall match you, Itadori Yuji?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.75,0:07:17.08,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Since he has admitted to entering the premises,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.08,0:07:22.51,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,judging from this photo, \Nhis bathroom excuse does not seem credible.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.01,0:07:28.80,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,We can conclude that, despite being underage, \NItadori entered the parlor with the intent to play.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.14,0:07:31.60,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,So...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.26,0:07:33.72,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,What am I guilty of?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.72,0:07:38.77,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Since the establishment explicitly prohibits \Nminors from entering,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.31,0:07:41.48,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,it's unlawful entry.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.36,0:07:44.03,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Article 130 of the Penal Code. {<- this is the standard legal phrasing} {CR: Penal Code, Article 130.}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.49,0:07:48.41,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,You see, minors can't be punished\Nunder the Entertainment Business Act. {Under the Entertainment Business Control Act, \Nminors can't be punished after all.} {CR: The Businesses Affecting Public Morals Regulation Act doesn't punish minors, after all.} {wtf cr?} {the idea here is that yuji would not have been punished for gambling anyway, not directly at least, thanks to the entertainment biz laws, which is why higuruma made him admit to unlawful entry}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.78,0:07:51.83,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,That wasn't fair.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.83,0:07:54.37,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,There was no talking my way out of it. {CR: There was no way to talk my way out of it.} {if only there was a way...}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.37,0:07:56.12,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}Should I have gone with option three?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.12,0:07:58.04,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,What are you talking about?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.04,0:08:00.33,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Gambling is illegal in Japan,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.33,0:08:03.13,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,so parlors and cash exchanges \Nare separate legal entities.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.50,0:08:06.42,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Sometimes multiple parlors even share one.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.42,0:08:11.05,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,You were only on trial for entry into Maji Vegas.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.51,0:08:13.10,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,You simply needed to say,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.10,0:08:18.02,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,"I don't know anything about that place," \Nand deny the accusation.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.06,0:08:21.40,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Wait, we haven't heard the verdict yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.95,0:08:29.20,Default,Judgeman,0,0,0,,{\an8}Guilty.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.20,0:08:30.70,Default,Judgeman,0,0,0,,{\an8}Confiscation.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.78,0:08:35.75,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}We're back to where we were?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.20,0:08:39.71,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}I was declared guilty, but I don't feel any different.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.71,0:08:39.83,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}I was declared guilty, but I don't feel any different.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.83,0:08:39.96,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\pos(1142,1040)\i1}I was declared guilty, but I don't feel any different.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.96,0:08:40.04,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\pos(1379,1080)\i1}I was declared guilty, but I don't feel any different.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.92,0:08:50.09,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}What the—
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.81,0:08:58.93,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}Not only can he summon and dismiss \Nthat gavel whenever he wants,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.93,0:09:00.94,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}he can change its size too?!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.35,0:09:02.94,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}No, there's a bigger problem...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.06,0:09:05.52,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,You're tough.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.19,0:09:08.49,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,That's the one thing I've got going for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.66,0:09:14.58,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}I can't control my cursed energy!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.37,0:09:30.72,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,Higuruma Hiromi, 36, of the Iwate Bar Association\Nand the 59th judicial trainee class. {CR: Law apprenticeship period 59. Iwate Bar Association's Higuruma Hiromi, age 36.}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.72,0:09:33.96,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,He cleared every challenge \Non his first try—
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.96,0:09:37.68,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,from the entrance exam \Nfor Tokyo University's law program
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.68,0:09:40.48,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,to the national bar exam \Npredating the law school system. {He readily overcame challenges like the entrance exam for Tokyo University's law school and the national bar exam that preceded the law school system.} {CR: He straightforwardly cleared all obstacles, like the entrance exam to Tokyo University's School of Law and the old bar exam that preceded the law school system.}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.48,0:09:43.48,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,To Higuruma, \Nit was simply a matter of
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.48,0:09:50.24,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,taking in whatever knowledge he needed\Nand recalling it whenever required.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.24,0:09:56.66,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,"Genius," those around him would whisper.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.66,0:10:04.17,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,Yet the brightest gem hidden within him\Nwas his talent as a sorcerer. {insane levels of glazing}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.38,0:10:14.51,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,While analyzing his technique, which came with a domain, \Nhe learned the fundamentals of barrier techniques as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.30,0:10:22.31,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,Working backwards, he got a feel for \Nreinforcement through cursed energy manipulation.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.31,0:10:29.40,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,Within twelve days of awakening, \Nhe had grown to be on par with first-grade sorcerers.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.15,0:10:34.45,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,Before entering the colony, \Nhe exorcised numerous cursed spirits.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.45,0:10:36.82,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,He then defeated over \Ntwenty players who came at him.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.82,0:10:36.87,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,{\clip(m 1094.86 859.43 l 1108.57 906.29 1120 952 1147.43 1062.86 1598.86 1068.57 1650.29 841.14)}He then defeated over \Ntwenty players who came at him.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.87,0:10:40.04,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,He then defeated over \Ntwenty players who came at him.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.28,0:11:19.91,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,You lost the ability to control cursed energy?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.12,0:11:22.70,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,You did this, didn't you?!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.20,0:11:29.34,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,The penalty of Confiscation makes it impossible \Nto use one's cursed technique for a time.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.79,0:11:33.42,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,I suspect you don't have a cursed technique.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.21,0:11:38.93,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,That must be why the penalty switched to \Nblocking the use of cursed energy.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.64,0:11:44.93,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Generally speaking, Confiscation is a supplementary \Nsentence that's never imposed by itself.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.89,0:11:48.69,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}It's terrifying to think about.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.44,0:11:53.15,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}How can he hold his own against me \Nwithout cursed energy?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.86,0:11:57.40,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}It's not his sorcery, \Nbut the body he was born with.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.40,0:12:00.37,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}His natural toughness is unbelievable.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.16,0:12:04.16,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}When sorcerers lose the use of their technique,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.16,0:12:07.37,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}they often struggle with \Nbasic cursed energy manipulation.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.92,0:12:10.54,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}Years of relying on their technique \Ndull their instincts.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.54,0:12:14.38,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}But the complete inability to use cursed energy \Nis an even greater disadvantage!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.84,0:12:17.72,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}He's putting up quite a fight despite all that.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.38,0:12:22.60,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}My first strike would have \Nsettled the battle against most foes.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.60,0:12:25.81,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}If I'm not careful, he'll trip me up.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.93,0:12:28.52,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'll crush him with everything I've got!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.69,0:13:10.69,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,You're incredible!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.44,0:13:14.40,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}It's like I'm fighting an indestructible doll.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.98,0:13:15.36,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}Shit!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.36,0:13:15.65,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}Shit, shit!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.65,0:13:15.94,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}Shit, shit, shit!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.94,0:13:16.23,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}Shit, shit, shit, shit!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.23,0:13:16.94,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}Shit, shit, shit, shit, shit!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.94,0:13:18.44,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}How long is this gonna last?!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.44,0:13:21.16,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}My cursed energy! \NHurry back to me, cursed energy!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.66,0:13:25.53,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}An ability this strong has to have an Achilles' heel! {"but he says higuruma why are you calling him achilles!"}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.53,0:13:27.16,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}Something I can use against him!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.70,0:13:29.91,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}Think!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.91,0:13:30.62,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}Think, think!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.62,0:13:31.12,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}Think, think, think!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.17,0:13:34.17,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}A technique based on court trials...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:34.17,0:13:35.29,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}Trials!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.09,0:13:44.26,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Higuruma!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.26,0:13:46.72,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,I want a retrial! One more time!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.52,0:13:58.03,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,You figured it out?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.44,0:14:01.90,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,That was close.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.90,0:14:04.49,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,I-I get a second trial, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.57,0:14:11.00,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,If Judgeman declares someone guilty \Nand imposes a penalty,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:11.00,0:14:17.34,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,they can request up to two retrials \Nas long as they haven't admitted their guilt.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.84,0:14:21.47,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,Judgeman cannot refuse.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.88,0:14:26.01,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,All right, one more time!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.10,0:14:31.27,Default,Judgeman,0,0,0,,Itadori Yuji
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.27,0:14:38.94,Default,Judgeman,0,0,0,,stands accused of mass murder in Shibuya \Non October 31st, 2018.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.03,0:14:44.11,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Yeah, I killed them.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.66,0:14:46.41,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,It's true. I won't deny it.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.24,0:14:50.79,Default,Judgeman,0,0,0,,{\an8}Guilty!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.79,0:14:52.79,Default,Judgeman,0,0,0,,{\an8}Confiscation!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.79,0:14:56.50,Default,Judgeman,0,0,0,,{\an8}Death Penalty!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.29,0:15:00.55,Default,Yoshizawa,0,0,0,,Higuruma{**-kun}.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.76,0:15:08.05,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,{*}Mr. Yoshizawa{*Yoshizawa-san}.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.97,0:15:12.14,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,If it's about the draft, I've already submitted it.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.73,0:15:15.94,Default,Yoshizawa,0,0,164,,Oh, it's not about that.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.94,0:15:18.86,Default,Yoshizawa,0,0,164,,I read the draft. It's excellent.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.36,0:15:22.61,Default,Yoshizawa,0,0,164,,Good enough to be used as-is for the ruling.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.11,0:15:28.70,Default,Yoshizawa,0,0,164,,You wanted to be either a prosecutor \Nor a defense lawyer, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.37,0:15:30.33,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.95,0:15:32.24,Default,Yoshizawa,0,0,164,,What do you say?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.62,0:15:36.25,Default,Yoshizawa,0,0,164,,Why not aim to become a judge?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.67,0:15:49.97,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,{\an8}This is the harshest sentence Judgeman can impose.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.97,0:15:54.22,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,{\an8}Death Penalty supplemented with Confiscation.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.93,0:16:03.78,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,{\an8}Confiscation makes it impossible to use one's technique, \Nor in Itadori's case, his cursed energy.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.78,0:16:08.03,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,{\an8}At the same time, Higuruma is granted \Nthe Executioner's Sword.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.57,0:16:16.33,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,{\an8}Anyone struck by the Executioner's Sword will, \Nwithout exception, meet their death.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.29,0:16:23.17,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}To empathize with someone is to understand their weakness.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.67,0:16:27.55,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}Weakness of the victims. Weakness of the criminals.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.47,0:16:31.43,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}Day after day after day...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.30,0:16:34.35,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}I was so fed up.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.43,0:16:36.93,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}"How ugly."
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.93,0:16:41.44,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}That's what I began to think \Nevery time I tried to reach out to people. {the more he tried to understand people, the more he began to see them as ugly}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.15,0:16:44.19,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,You are no exception, Itadori!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.44,0:16:49.91,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,All people are weak and ugly!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.91,0:16:53.53,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,No matter how noble a soul you wish to be! {CR: No matter how much you long for them to have noble souls!} {nice tl error}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.24,0:16:58.46,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Nothing's waiting down that path! {he knows because he was once on the same path} {i want to rewrite this because it feels too stock but the "nothing" part just flows too well with darkness and void in the following lines}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.46,0:17:01.08,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,The darkness before you is just that—darkness! {darkness = guilt of the deaths he caused}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.17,0:17:07.05,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Shine a light and you'll {\i1}still{\i0} be left \Nwith a blinding void! {even if he atones for it, that won't bring him peace, it'll only leave him empty}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.51,0:17:14.64,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.18,0:17:16.10,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,I won't become a judge.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.10,0:17:17.77,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,I won't become a judge.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.48,0:17:23.77,Default,Yoshizawa,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.77,0:17:25.90,Default,Yoshizawa,0,0,0,,May I ask why not?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.19,0:17:30.32,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}All people are weak and ugly.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:32.66,0:17:36.54,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,I'm not cut out for it, \Nsince I'm not interested in promotions.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.54,0:17:40.46,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}At the time, however...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.46,0:17:42.50,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}At least up until that point...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.00,0:17:49.13,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}I believed that very impurity—\Nso uniquely human—was something to be cherished! {humans are weak and ugly -- but that's what makes them human} {it should also be noted that he's talking about weakness and ugliness of humans when he says impurity, and not his disinterest in promotions, because some translations got that idea and made it depravity} {and by some i mean both crunchy and viz}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.55,0:17:50.38,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}Why?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.34,0:17:52.47,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}Why, Itadori Yuji?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.18,0:17:55.26,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}Why did you admit guilt?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.64,0:18:02.94,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,The evidence provided by Judgeman \Nis shared with the sorcerer before it is opened. {so he just lied before when he said it's not shared with him?} {or maybe it's not shared with him until the trial is done, like just before opening}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.40,0:18:08.32,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}The evidence was about \Nthe demon dwelling within you—Sukuna!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.53,0:18:10.78,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}You didn't kill them!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.86,0:18:13.82,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}So why?! Why?!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.09,0:18:34.89,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Hey!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.30,0:18:39.60,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Article 39, Paragraph 1 of the Penal Code. {<- this is the standard legal phrasing} {Article 39, Paragraph 1 of the Penal Code.}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.72,0:18:47.31,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Being deprived of either sound judgment or control \Nof one's actions qualifies as non compos mentis. {"legally insane" but i get the feeling that it will be misinterpreted so latin it is}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.23,0:18:53.57,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,In Shibuya, Sukuna had taken control of your body.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.57,0:18:55.49,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,How do you know about Sukuna?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.28,0:18:59.33,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Meaning you lacked control of your actions.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.33,0:19:03.41,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,You didn't voluntarily surrender control, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.41,0:19:04.33,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,In other words,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:05.12,0:19:06.21,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,you're innocent.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:08.63,0:19:10.34,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,You've committed no crime.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:12.55,0:19:15.13,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Still, it's my fault.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.22,0:19:18.18,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Because I was too weak.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.14,0:19:23.48,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.31,0:19:28.23,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Higuruma, why did you release your technique?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:31.90,0:19:33.99,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,I returned to my roots.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:35.86,0:19:42.95,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Itadori, there may still be plenty of people \Nwith a weakness like yours. {weakness here refers to his honesty and not physical weakness}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:44.62,0:19:46.12,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Put your clothes on.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.12,0:19:47.67,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Then have a seat.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.67,0:19:49.29,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,I'll give you my 100 points.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:02.64,0:20:03.68,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Itadori.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.18,0:20:08.56,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Have you ever killed someone of your own volition?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.19,0:20:17.20,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,I have.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:23.16,0:20:24.08,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.29,0:20:28.42,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,It must have felt awful. {CR: It felt absolutely awful, didn't it?} {this kinda ties into the earlier lines: Have you ever killed someone who ticked you off? It feels better than you'd expect.}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:59.88,0:22:02.30,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Kogane, add a rule.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:03.22,0:22:07.10,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Make it possible for players \Nto transfer points to one another.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:07.93,0:22:12.73,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Of course, this should count toward \Nthe "change in points" mentioned in Rule 8.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:12.73,0:22:14.44,Default,Kogane,0,0,0,,Approved.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:14.94,0:22:21.19,Default,Kogane,0,0,0,,Rule 10: Players may transfer a number of points \Nof their choosing to another player.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:22.70,0:22:25.57,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Kogane, give one of my points to Itadori.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:26.12,0:22:27.70,Default,Kogane,0,0,0,,As you wish.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:29.70,0:22:33.21,Default,Kogane,0,0,0,,You have been granted one point \Nby Higuruma Hiromi.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:34.21,0:22:38.71,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Now neither of us will have to worry about \Nour technique being stripped for nineteen days.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:39.34,0:22:40.67,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Take care.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:41.26,0:22:42.30,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Higuruma!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:42.63,0:22:44.63,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,What are you planning to do now?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:44.63,0:22:47.22,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Would you be willing to help us?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:49.72,0:22:55.73,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,My two remaining points are from \Nthe judge and prosecutor I killed before coming here.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:56.98,0:23:00.44,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Once the barriers open up, I think I'll turn myself in.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:01.32,0:23:04.74,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Until then, I'll think about what I should do.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:05.45,0:23:10.08,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Besides, if I stay around you, \NI might end up hating myself even more.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:11.37,0:23:14.41,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Sorry, I didn't mean to blame you.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:15.92,0:23:16.92,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Later.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:25.68,0:23:27.34,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,{\an8}A new rule will be added soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:27.34,0:23:29.97,Default,Kogane,0,0,0,,{\an8}...a number of points \Nof their choosing to another player.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:29.97,0:23:31.60,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\an8}If you don't fight to kill...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:31.60,0:23:32.31,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,{\an8}You're okay with this?! {i have a feeling i'll have to change this line} {guess not}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:32.31,0:23:34.14,Default,Takaba,0,0,0,,{\an8}I don't want you as my Wi-Fi! {THE GOAT IS HERE! HELL YEAH!}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:34.14,0:23:36.81,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,{\an8}You'll hand over all your points.
